// spec: LEX-016
//
// A separator separates two DIGITS.  A trailing one has nothing to its right,
// so the literal ends before it and '_' starts an identifier [SRC-005] -- the
// number and the name are then two adjacent expressions, which do not parse.
//
// ⚠️ This is the same shape '0x10' had before hexadecimal arrived: a form that
// is not a literal does not become an error in the scanner, it becomes two
// tokens and fails in the parser.

WriteLn (100_);
